1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:07,610
The students are now asking Lily some questions after her talk.

2
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:16,020
Listen and complete the summary of Lily's answers below. Hi, Lily.

3
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:21,750
Thank you for sharing your English learning experience with us.

4
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:23,610
I have a question.

5
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:28,450
How important do you think pronunciation is?

6
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:34,870
Well, pronunciation is a big part of learning a language.

7
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:41,100
If you get the pronunciation wrong, people may not understand you.

8
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:53,100
Good pronunciation takes lots of practice, and doing just a little bit every day will be a big help.

9
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:58,150
Difficult to study grammar.

10
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:04,260
Yes, grammar can be hard to learn, but it is important.

11
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:09,300
We need the rules of a language to make sentences.

12
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,790
Try to write something in English every day.

13
00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:18,170
Can reading help us improve our English too?

14
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:22,820
Yes, but it's important to read often.

15
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:30,270
Start by reading easy texts and then slowly move on to more difficult ones.

16
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:34,020
You don't have to understand every word.

17
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:37,680
The more you read, the more you'll understand.
